{"task_id": "HumanEval/71", "solution": "import math\n\ndef triangle_area(a, b, c):\n    # Validate side lengths: must be positive\n    if a <= 0 or b <= 0 or c <= 0:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Check triangle inequality theorem: sum of any two sides must be greater than the third side\n    if not (a + b > c and a + c > b and b + c > a):\n        return -1\n    \n    # Calculate semi-perimeter\n    s = (a + b + c) / 2\n    \n    # Calculate area using Heron's formula, guarding against potential floating point errors\n    try:\n        area_squared = s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c)\n        # Ensure area_squared is not negative due to floating point inaccuracies, though it should be positive for a valid triangle\n        if area_squared < 0: \n            return -1 # Should ideally not happen if inputs are valid and not extremely pathological\n        \n        area = math.sqrt(area_squared)\n        return round(area, 2)\n    except Exception: # Catch potential errors from math.sqrt for robustness\n        return -1"}
